{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-33317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(1,-4,2)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,-3)$ and $B(1,6,-4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨1,-4,2⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,-3)$ and $B(1,6,-4)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,6,-4⟩-⟨2,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,5,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ & =⟨1,-4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "af62567032904ab0c11d2f92c78708763fc073d35840b55f5e8617b45657faaf"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=-23"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=0"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=⟨1,-4,2⟩"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩=-23"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩=⟨-1,5,-1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=-23"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨6,-2,0⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =0 \\\\ 6{t}_{1}-2{t}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},3{t}_{1},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ eqauls $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{1}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "af62567032904ab0c11d2f92c78708763fc073d35840b55f5e8617b45657faaf"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-70893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(4,-2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(-1,0,1)$ and $B(1,0,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-70893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨4,-2,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(-1,0,1)$ and $B(1,0,-1)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,0,-1⟩-⟨-1,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,0,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨2,0,-2⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩ & =⟨4,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩ & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-70893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "af62567032904ab0c11d2f92c78708763fc073d35840b55f5e8617b45657faaf"} {"question" "q-70893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-70893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩=0"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩=2"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩=⟨4,-2,3⟩"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨4,-2,3⟩=2"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨4,-2,3⟩=⟨2,0,-2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-70893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩=2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-127888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-1⟩=\\sqrt{2}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-127888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-1⟩=\\sqrt{2}$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨3,2,-1⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}-{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{3} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{2},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{2}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{2}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-127888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "af62567032904ab0c11d2f92c78708763fc073d35840b55f5e8617b45657faaf"} {"question" "q-127888" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-127888" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-127888" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-127936" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(3,-2,5)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(-3,0,2)$ and $B(2,1,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-127936" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,-2,5⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(-3,0,2)$ and $B(2,1,3)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,1,3⟩-⟨-3,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨5,1,1⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩ & =⟨3,-2,5⟩\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩ & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-127936" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "af62567032904ab0c11d2f92c78708763fc073d35840b55f5e8617b45657faaf"} {"question" "q-127936" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "82e4aef0512910c4b752072173cd39d128d68e693013fa89d8bf9761bb905e26"} {"question" "q-127936" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,5⟩=9"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨1,3,1⟩=12"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨1,5,1⟩=9"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨3,1,1⟩=12"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩=18"]] 